481	\begin{proof}
482		\leanok
483		\uses{def:admissible}
484		Write $D=md$, and set $\beta=b/8$, $A=4C^2a$, $H=aD^a$, and
485		$R=\eps^\beta+q^{-\beta}+2^{-\beta D}$.
486		Admissibility gives $D,q\geq1$, so $H\geq D\geq1$, $A\geq a>1$,
487		and $0<\beta<1$. Fourth-root subadditivity and monotonicity of real
488		powers, using $0\leq\eps\leq1$ and $\beta\leq b/4$, give
489		\[
490			\delta_G^{1/4}\leq HR,\qquad
491			\eps^{1/8}\leq HR,\qquad
492			(D/q)^{1/4}\leq HR,\qquad D/q\leq HR.
493		\]
494		Indeed, the fourth root of the sum defining $\delta_G/H$ is at most
495		$R$, while $H^{1/4}\leq H$, $D^{1/4}\leq D\leq H$,
496		$\eps^{1/8}\leq\eps^\beta$, and $q^{-1/4},q^{-1}\leq q^{-\beta}$.
